Local patch applied to CAPD 6.1.0 (commit 03dc5628203334b214bb7d9fd63788a175521005) on 2026-10-01 with the owner's approval.
The file uses CRLF line endings; apply with `git apply` from the CAPD source root (header only, no library rebuild).

In crossSectionInOneStep, each Newton iteration sets bound = c(newReturnTime) and checks the sign of every component of
the vector field on that bound, then intersected bound[j] with the hull of the curve at the endpoints of the PREVIOUS
window. That trim is valid only on the window where monotonicity was checked; the windows coincide when the loop exits
by convergence but not when it stops at its 10-iteration cap. The patch takes the endpoints of the current window.

